{"title":"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 37","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two equal parallel chords are drawn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches apart in a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches. The area of that part of the circle that lies between the chords is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/d/2bd24c83df0bbba43750aa2af9a2a32abd2507b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 21\\frac{1}{3}\\pi-32\\sqrt{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 32\\sqrt{3}+21\\frac{1}{3}\\pi\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 32\\sqrt{3}+42\\frac{2}{3}\\pi \\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ 16\\sqrt {3} + 42\\frac {2}{3}\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 42\\frac {2}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"489\" height=\"75\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/344851cbf1cd627a82344a8ad91aaeaada984e20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G; A=(0,0); B=(-5,4sqrt(3)+2); C=(5,4sqrt(3)+2); D=(-5,-4sqrt(3)-0.5); E=(5,-4sqrt(3)-0.5); F=(-4,0); G=(4,-sqrt(2)/2); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,-0.5),S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,W); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,NE); draw(circle(A,8));  draw((-4,-4sqrt(3))--(-4,4sqrt(3))); draw((4,-4sqrt(3))--(4,4sqrt(3))); draw((-4,-4sqrt(3))--(4,4sqrt(3))); draw((4,-4sqrt(3))--(-4,4sqrt(3))); draw((4,0)--(-4,0)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(-2.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(2.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(-2.5,3)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(2.5,3)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(-2.5,-3)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(2.5,-3)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"252\" />\nDraw in the diameter through A perpendicular to chords BD and CE. Label the intersection points of the diameter with the chords F and G. Then, AF=4, AG=4, and AFB ,AFD, AEG. and AGC are right triangles. We're going to find the area inside sectors BAD and CAE but outside triangles BAD and CAE.\n</p><p>By pythagorean theorem, BF=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bddfa0dd561449e70720e765113a3c75dc6382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />, as are DF, EG, and GC.\n</p><p>It then follows that the area of triangles BAD and CAE are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580fa51087efd01969f8ad190ace7038c99fd137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Since AFB and AFD are 30-60-90 triangles, the area of sector BAD is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a08d4ebaf370907c2581ccd2942bb53393ec164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" />, as is sector CAE.\n</p><p>Thus, the area outside of the two chords is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2cc04e0b6b770c0e51fafbfe3d51c89ee6520c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{128\\pi}{3}-32\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" />.\nSince we want the area inside the two chords, you can subtract the outside from the whole circle, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320ad0ba607721744d77846dc3b951ee9c736a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64\\pi-(\\frac{128\\pi}{3}-32\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"171\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65fbb399c33e72d4c4bf7bea245fbf449e75a56a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\frac{64\\pi}{3}+32\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />, or \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area inside the chords are the arcs plus the triangles. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d59b1384670dfc0b60fb9b4f6610e37e3f8c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328703d8157a5761b4ff513fb0165c991d1d9781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are 30-60-90 triangles, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8cc282b5d9bb4dfc397f1b13d8f8b3e4f6f0ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\angle DAE = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />. This means that the sum of the sectors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc7ed4627c8f52fa4994ce847bcc42df775d31d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64 \\pi} {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"35\" height=\"38\" />. The triangles are both equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46aa86232f61232474c9d0e6e98fcd58d5e060d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8\\sqrt{3} \\cdot 4} {2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"43\" />, so the sum of the two is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb091bfa9be998f89ca94c53b39b17e531a62d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Finally, we add the two together. This yields the answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b2aa6dcfaca5614cbf883f6ddb49adc03646d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64\\pi}{3}+32\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~clever14710owl\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Step 1: Finding the Height</b>\n</p><p>We have a triangle with a slant side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a base half-length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem, the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16bd7cfdb2e2addd02a460729caa2b4db9c88622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 = 8^2 - 4^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb56b42cf8296f9b97be02945b7d5486750289b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h = \\sqrt{8^2 - 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 - 16} = \\sqrt{48} = \\sqrt{16 \\cdot 3} = 4\\sqrt{3}.\\]\" width=\"401\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><b>Step 2: Finding the Angles</b>\n</p><p>Using the cosine ratio between the half-base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb996ca207df5d210cd86914aed764adb55fcb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> and the slant side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/32202bd01a7377981c667f014d641c6fad5b7aca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{8} = \\frac{1}{2} \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\theta = 60^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"37\" />\nThe full apex angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c4a4fd6bfcdefda3c2e0e4897b6baa8256b8812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\theta = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, so the sector angle is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2332f244ab5086775c94ceb03af2cf441974e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta&#39; = 180^\\circ - 120^\\circ = 60^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>Step 3: Area of the Triangles</b>\n</p><p>Four congruent triangles, each base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bddfa0dd561449e70720e765113a3c75dc6382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294885c99b22e1c27d05f56e36e561f26d435aef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area}_\\triangle = 4 \\times \\tfrac{1}{2} \\times 4\\sqrt{3} \\times 4 = 32\\sqrt{3}.\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><b>Step 4: Area of the Sectors</b>\n</p><p>Each sector has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93ed7100a37e0240d8ab1d2cc87091bde02c5396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 8$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and spans <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5364333ba9946f5ee9373f149ec118f36e9fd16f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ = \\tfrac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"62\" height=\"23\" /> of a circle:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b0981d9595e177293521aaa80ead8c8240232c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\pi (8)^2 = \\frac{128\\pi}{6} = \\frac{64\\pi}{3}.\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><b>Step 5: Final Total Area</b>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5dbbdcb40eadee9176af3a095d851b1319c900.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{32\\sqrt{3} + \\frac{64\\pi}{3}}\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Yuvraaj Verma\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME\" title=\"1952 AHSME\">1952 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1952 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1952\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 36\">Problem 36</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 38\">Problem 38</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1952 AHSME Proble